# Reference only. Nothing in this repository loads a .env file, and nothing needs to:
# `pnpm backend:dev` starts one backend per company and sets all of this for each of them, because
# the values differ per company. They act as different organisations, listen on different ports,
# and four of them hold no database at all.
#
# To run a single backend by hand, put the variables on the command line:
#
#   ORGANISATION=oracle pnpm --filter @fresh-milk/backend dev:one

# Which company this process acts for, and so which private key it signs with. Required.
# One of: regulator, farm, processor, logistics, retailer, oracle.
ORGANISATION=oracle

# There is no PORT. Each company's port comes from the table in
# services/backend/src/organisations.ts, so six processes reading one .env cannot all try to bind
# the same socket.

# Only the oracle and the regulator keep off-chain data, in separate databases. Leave this unset
# for the other four: no connection string is the correct configuration for a company that stores
# nothing, and the routes that serve stored rows answer 503.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://oracle_app:oracle@localhost:5432/freshmilk_oracle
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://regulator_app:regulator@localhost:5432/freshmilk_regulator

FABRIC_CHANNEL_NAME=milkchannel

# Written by the regulator's listener only, so a restart resumes rather than replaying the chain.
EVENT_CHECKPOINT_PATH=.fabric-events.regulator.checkpoint

# Where the oracle's backend is. The oracle publishes the readings, and every other company fetches
# them from here to check them against the ledger itself.
# ORACLE_BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:3006

# Where the oracle process sends the evidence it anchors: its own backend, the only one holding the
# oracle's certificate.
# BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:3006

# The network lives in this repository, so these are only needed to point somewhere else.
# FABRIC_NETWORK_PATH=./fabric/milk-network
# FABRIC_ORGANIZATIONS_PATH=./fabric/milk-network/organizations/peerOrganizations

# Where Fabric's binaries and default core.yaml were installed.
# FABRIC_SAMPLES_HOME=~/fabric-samples
